WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:07.020
A private AI assistant is an end-to-end system, not merely a local model.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.278
Infrastructure, interfaces, knowledge, retrieval, logs, backups, integrations, access,

00:00:11.278 --> 00:00:14.472
and administration determine its actual privacy.

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:20.327
Start with a narrow purpose, defined audience, permitted data, prohibited actions,

00:00:20.327 --> 00:00:21.924
and measurable success.

00:00:21.924 --> 00:00:27.779
Choose hardware, model, quantization, runtime, and interface according to that workload.

00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:33.102
Ground private knowledge through controlled ingestion, retrieval evaluation, source citations,

00:00:33.102 --> 00:00:34.698
versioning, and authorization.

00:00:34.698 --> 00:00:40.554
Design the interface for usability, correction, transparent history, and human escalation.

00:00:40.554 --> 00:00:45.876
Secure accounts, APIs, networks, secrets, downloads, prompts, documents, indexes, logs,

00:00:45.876 --> 00:00:46.941
and backups.

00:00:46.941 --> 00:00:52.264
Evaluate the complete workflow for quality, hallucination, latency, memory, stability,

00:00:52.264 --> 00:00:53.861
permission, and recovery.

00:00:53.861 --> 00:01:00.780
Start small, measure real value, and expand only when the assistant reliably helps.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:06.103
Strong assistants are useful, maintainable, secure, grounded, honest about uncertainty,

00:01:06.103 --> 00:01:07.700
and appropriately limited.
